**This is the unlock.** Line 1249's `spi_flash_read` is gated by `CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPI_FLASH_DONT_USE_ROM_CODE` (the closing `#endif` proves it), and it's currently **off** — so we've been getting the broken ROM routine. The NuttX software version does exactly what we need:

```c
spiflash_start();
for (...) {
  uint32_t spi_buffer[SPI_BUFFER_WORDS];      // internal-SRAM bounce, on stack
  READ_DATA_FROM_FLASH(rx_addr, spi_buffer, n);  // real SPI read — no ROM, no MMU
  if (buffer_in_psram) spiflash_resume_cache();   // ...and it HANDLES PSRAM dest itself!
  memcpy(rx_buf, spi_buffer, n);
  if (buffer_in_psram) spiflash_suspend_cache();
}
```

**No `esp32s3_mmap` (→ no -ENOBUFS), no ROM (→ no 24577), and it toggles the cache around the PSRAM copy automatically.** It even detects `buffer_in_psram` — so I can read straight into the PSRAM model buffer, no manual bounce. Enabling `DONT_USE_ROM_CODE` also makes it a strong symbol that overrides the ROM `PROVIDE`.

