Still black — so a real hardware CS didn't unlock it either. That was the last untested hypothesis. Let me be straight with you: **I've now exhausted everything that can be tested by flashing.** Confirmed working: power, panel, init, pins, forced pin-mux, DMA-off/poll, and now dummy hardware CS. The esp32s3 SPI2 core simply emits nothing on the wire, and the driver code is correct on inspection.

**This is a fault that needs a logic analyzer** — probe GPIO5 (CLK) and GPIO1 (MOSI) while the peripheral fires and see whether they actually toggle. That's a 5-minute answer with a $10 analyzer and an unbounded guessing game without one. I'd be wasting your time to keep blind-flashing.

